 #define MAX_QUEUE_LENGTH 10000
 
+/* How many stanzas may go out before we ask to have them acknowledged, and how long we wait
+   for a quieter moment before asking anyway.
+
+   Upstream asks after every single one, which doubles the number of stanzas on the wire for
+   no gain: the acknowledgement carries a running total, so one answer settles everything sent
+   before it. What the asking is actually for is knowing what to send again after a break, and
+   for that it only has to happen often enough that the queue stays small and the tail of a
+   conversation does not sit unacknowledged.
+
+   The timer is what makes a threshold safe. Without it a handful of stanzas below the
+   threshold would never be asked about at all, and after a reconnection they would go out a
+   second time although the server had them. */
+#define REQUEST_AFTER_STANZAS 5
+#define REQUEST_AFTER_SECONDS 2
+
+/* How long a probe may go unanswered before the connection is called lost.
+ *
+ * A write alone does not settle it. A socket whose other end has gone without saying so accepts
+ * what is written into the kernel's buffer and reports nothing; only the retransmissions run
+ * out, minutes later. What does settle it is the silence: a server that is there answers an
+ * <r/> in well under a second, so ten is generous and still an age next to the fifty-nine
+ * seconds this was measured costing. */
+#define PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 10
+
